# Ink deploy canary. Claude rewrites this file after a substantial change; InkWatch (scripts\ink-watch.ps1)
# notices the new modification time and runs scripts\ink-push.ps1: commit + push, Firestore rules, Worker.
# subject: becomes the commit subject; everything after body: becomes the commit body.
last_tick: 2026-09-18T11:45:00Z
subject: Fix bold/italic breaking across paragraphs (toolbar + renderer)
body:
- Root cause: render.js pairs **/* markers only WITHIN a single paragraph (it splits the body into blocks on blank lines before it ever inspects markers). The new toolbar's wrap button only placed the marker at the outer edges of the selection, so selecting more than one paragraph and clicking Bold/Italic stranded an opening marker in the first paragraph and a closing one in the last, with nothing to pair against in either -- exactly the "shows up literally" bug from the screenshot.
- Fix: edWrap() now wraps every paragraph inside the selection separately, so multi-paragraph selections (a whole italicized excerpt, for example) always render correctly.
- Also fixed italic in render.js itself to allow a soft line break (single \n) inside the emphasis, matching how bold already worked -- a real paragraph break (blank line) still can never be crossed, since renderBlocks() splits on that before inline() runs.
- Cleaned up the toolbar CSS (the group divider lines looked misaligned once the buttons wrapped to a second row on a narrower screen).
